To terminate a C program, you can use the `exit()` function. This function takes an integer argument, which is the status of the program. The program will then exit with that status code. Here's an example:

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    // Your program code here
    printf("Hello, world!\n");
    // Exit the program with status 0
    exit(0);
}
```

In this example, the program will print "Hello, world!" and then exit with status 0. If you want to exit with a different status code, you can pass that as
